    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Loading and securing for car transport on train or open vehicle transport</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Align the vehicle on the carrier’s ramp using the manufacturer’s recommended wheel‑chock points. Secure with ratchet straps at the front axle, rear axle, and undercarriage, tightening to the specified torque. Double‑check that the straps do not interfere with the battery terminals or fuel cap, and confirm clearance with the train’s loading gauge or the open trailer’s height limits.</p>
