    <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.65); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 16px; padding: 36px 32px; box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);">
      <span style="background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.12); color: #f59e0b; border: 1px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">HANDOVER INSPECTION</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Car Transportation In Fatehpur Chaurasi</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>At the destination, the handover of an automobile or car is a structured, three‑step process designed to ensure the vehicle’s condition, mileage, and ownership records are verified before the final sign‑off. First, a daylight re‑inspection is conducted by the receiving agent, who compares the vehicle’s exterior and interior against the original pickup photographs.</p>
<p>This visual audit confirms that no new damage has occurred during transit and that any pre‑existing issues remain unchanged. The agent records any discrepancies in a digital log, attaching side‑by‑side photo evidence to the delivery report.</p>

<p>Second, the vehicle’s odometer reading is cross‑checked against the mileage listed on the LR (Logistics Receipt) bilty. The driver’s signed mileage declaration is read, and the reading is verified with the vehicle’s instrument cluster.</p>
<p>Any variance beyond a pre‑approved tolerance (typically ±5 km) triggers an immediate investigation, which may involve a third‑party mileage verification service. Once confirmed, the mileage is entered into the system and stamped on the delivery docket, ensuring a single source of truth for all parties.</p>

<p>Third, a signed condition sign‑off is obtained from the recipient. The handover form includes a checklist of key vehicle parameters—body panels, tires, fluid levels, and safety equipment—mirroring the pickup inspection checklist. The recipient reviews each item, marks it as “OK” or “Not OK,” and signs the document.</p>
<p>The delivery agent then affixes their signature, creating a legally binding record that the vehicle was received in the documented condition. All signed documents, photographs, and mileage logs are stored electronically and forwarded to the central fleet management system, closing the delivery loop and enabling audit trails for future reference.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



